#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example shows a Braking Distance Test for an E-Class Sedan with pedal force input, power boost, and thermal effects.
#
#In this test procedure, the car is traveling at 102 km/h at the start of the simulation and coasts down to 100  km/h.  Using Events, the car is repositioned to the start of the road (0 m) and simultaneously begins to brake. Review the plot of Station vs. Time to measure the vehicle's braking distance.
#
#NOTE: This example was provided in older versions of CarSim to demonstrate an alternative brake library screen. In the newer versions (2017), the standard 4W brake system screen is used to set the options.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

